    {
      "text": "Isaiah, who spake concerning the restoration of the Jews, 1 Ne. 15:20. day cometh … that they no more turn aside their hearts, 1 Ne. 19:15. they shall be brought out of obscurity, 1 Ne. 22:12. bringing to pass much restoration unto the house of Israel, 2 Ne. 3:24. shall come to the knowledge of their Redeemer, 2 Ne. 6:11. they shall be restored to the true church and fold, 2 Ne. 9:2. When … they shall believe in me … they shall be restored, 2 Ne. 10:7. to restore his people from their lost and fallen state, 2 Ne. 25:17. set my hand again the second time to recover my people, 2 Ne. 29:1 (Jacob 6:2). to bring about the restoration of his people, 2 Ne. 30:8. have brought unto me again the natural fruit, Jacob 5:75. bring a remnant … of Joseph to the knowledge of the Lord, 3 Ne. 5:23. may be brought to a knowledge of me, their Redeemer, 3 Ne. 16:4. they shall believe in me, that I am Jesus Christ, 3 Ne. 20:31. to prepare the way whereby they may come unto me, 3 Ne. 21:27. Jews … may be persuaded that Jesus is the Christ, Morm. 5:14. Ether … spake concerning a New Jerusalem upon this land, Ether 13:4. awake, and arise from the dust, O Jerusalem, Moro. 10:31.",
